From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_balloon: back off when inflation makes zero progress

With ~1ms stall retries plus drop-caches-on-stall, a balloon that has
taken everything reclaimable never converges: fill_balloon() burns
through a flusher kick plus two system-wide drop_caches() in ~2ms,
returns 0, and update_balloon_size_func() requeues immediately because
diff is still nonzero. The guest then spins hundreds of global cache
drops per second forever while making no progress (and the host never
gets another page).

Sleep the stock 200ms when a batch allocated nothing, so the stuck
case retries at ~5Hz instead of ~500Hz. Batches that made any progress
keep the fast path and converge as before; a guest that later frees
memory is still picked up on a retry a fraction of a second later.

No behaviour change while progress is being made.

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
index 123456789025..123456789026 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -321,6 +321,14 @@
 	if (vb->num_pfns != 0)
 		tell_host(vb, vb->inflate_vq);
 	mutex_unlock(&vb->balloon_lock);
+	/*
+	 * Zero progress means only unreclaimable memory is left; back off
+	 * to the stock cadence so the outer requeue does not spin doing
+	 * system-wide drop_caches() hundreds of times per second forever.
+	 * Batches that made progress keep the ~1ms fast path above.
+	 */
+	if (!num_allocated_pages)
+		msleep(200);
 
 	return num_allocated_pages;
 }
